    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17616" root="زر" body-key="z">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">زِرَّةٌ</span></b>  The <i>mark left by a bite:</i> (K, TA:) or, as
some say, <i>a bite itself.</i> (TA.) And <i>A wound
with the edge of a sword.</i> (TA.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  J says, When
camels are fat, you say, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بِهَا زِرَّةٌ</span>: but this is a mistake for <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَهَا زِرَةٌ</span>, (Sgh, K,) which is pl. of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بُهْزُورَةٌ</span>.
(TA in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بهزر</span>.)

